WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.100
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.100
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.700
Dr. Eggman, I finished repairing the main engine.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.040
The control device is also finished.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.250
Alright! But why did it take two weeks?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.340
It's because they were having fun and ignoring us!

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.510
It's ridiculous! Did they forget that this TV show is on air thanks to us?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:01.760
I mean - it's on air thanks to Dr. Eggman.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.390
As long as you understand.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.810
You better watch what you say.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.640
They won't remove our characters from the show starting next week, will they?

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.480
Start the engines! We're going to punish Sonic right away!

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.900
Right!

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.820
Increase the output of the sub engine! Ignite the main engine!

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.910
Do I have to say that out loud?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.620
Well, that's how it's always done…

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.500
Huh?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.330
What's going on?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.210
Dr. Eggman, did you finish repairing the energy transfer system?

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.590
Are you doubting my technique?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.010
Pardon me for my rudeness.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.590
Huh?

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.300
Something's wrong.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:48.350
Even the best swimmers drown, and monkeys fall from trees. Similarly, even I occasionally make mistakes.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.390
What?

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.860
Okay, we're going to build a new robot today named Egg Fort II!

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.990
What?

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:03.140
Episode 20

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:03.140
Departure! Egg Fort II

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:13.330
After daily vicious battles against Dr. Eggman for the Chaos Emeralds, our minds and bodies are exhausted. What we need is…

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.090
Time to relax, right?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:24.010
Then you need to take a relaxing cruise. I'm not using one of my smaller boats, so you should take it and go see the glaciers.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:29.100
So that's how we ended up on this relaxing voyage, but...

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.690
It's been three days since we set sail, but in order to reach the northern lands where we can see the glaciers, we still have...

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.940
Four more days!

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.690
We're finally halfway there.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.150
This voyage sure is slow.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.110
Hey Chris, did I wrong you somehow?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.830
Tell it to me straight. I'll mend my ways! I'll do whatever you say!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.120
Sonic.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:55.380
I beg you, let's go home. Let me go home!

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.630
That night…

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.920
That is a problem.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.010
Grandpa, are you really thinking?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:09.520
Of course I am! Do I look like I'm feeling good because I've had too much to drink?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.350
Yes.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.690
Well, pardon me. Hahaha!

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.310
Sheesh, are all adults like this?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:22.320
Hey Chris, do we really have to relax and be lazy?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.070
No, you don't have to if you don't want to.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.620
Why can't men be gracious and gorgeous?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:34.790
That's right. Chris's father went through all the trouble to give us this wonderful boat as a present.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.210
I-I'm having fun.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.380
Really?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.720
Maybe I'm a little bit bored.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.300
We can manage, but it's a problem for Sonic.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:52.270
This ship is too small for Sonic. At this rate, he'll go nuts.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.350
I think he's already gone nuts.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.810
He's running around the ship at supersonic speed.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.940
Amazing.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:03.900
He's now harder to control than the power of a Chaos Emerald.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.360
Well, let's check.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.620
Stop!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.450
Sonic, can you hear me?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.870
Yes I can.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.370
How old are you?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.210
Fifteen.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.420
Then you should be able to understand the situation you're in.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:25.260
As the star of this TV show and a hero to the world, your actions are what keeps Sonic X going.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.140
Not to mention the TV ratings and merchandise sales.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.140
Are you aware of the number of people who rely on you?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.640
That's why you have to act like a hero.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:40.690
So you're stuck on a ship surrounded by water and can't run around for a week. That's no big deal.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.190
I think it is a big deal for Sonic.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.110
Yeah.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.530
You're troubling everyone on this trip with your selfishness.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.250
He's sulking! The hero's sulking!

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.840
See! I told you he's not acting normal!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.920
I'll call my father.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:12.100
Oh well, sorry. You all take it easy and enjoy yourselves. See you.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.140
Sheesh, he's totally back to normal again.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:19.730
It can't be helped. It would've been cruel if we let Sonic go even more insane.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.690
I'll see you all later.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.240
Wow, it's the real thing.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.910
It's Sonic.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.740
You're right. How incredible!

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.410
I'm lucky to have lived this long.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.910
What's going on?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.210
Good morning, everyone.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.880
Tanaka.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.420
What's going on? Who are those elderly people?

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:54.100
They're from the Silver Star Home. Mr. Thorndyke asked them to coach you on this trip.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.760
Coach?

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.890
Coach us on what?

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.350
On how to relax.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:09.190
They're professionals at relaxing, so you youngsters are going to learn how to truly relax.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.240
Wait a sec. I asked father to come pick Sonic up.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.080
That is not allowed.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:24.170
A true warrior needs rest. If he continues to go all out, not only will he wear out his body, but also his mind.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.760
A single attack from a relaxed pose is...

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.300
Yes, that would have been a fatal blow.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.220
Hey, wait up!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.320
No! Come back!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.860
Starting that day, we were taught how to relax.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:08:04.880
Reading a book is nice, but my favorite thing to do is look up at the sky and watch the clouds drift by.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:22.940
I see. You're from another world.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.190
Yes, we used to live in a place called Green Hill.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:31.190
Oh, I see. How cute.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.820
Thank you.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.570
So what's your name?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.910
My name is Cream.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:42.250
You have a delicious-sounding name.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.000
So where are you from?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:51.380
We used to live in another world, but something terrible happened, and we were sent to this world.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:57.090
I see. You're from another world.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.100
That's right.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:02.390
Cream and Cheese spent all morning and afternoon talking about the same thing over and over.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.980
Sonic tried jumping off the boat for the fifteenth time that day.

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.620
Captain, he's about 9.5 kilometers away.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.700
That's his best record today.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.620
Geez, he never gives up.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:30.000
And I thought I could have a nice relaxing talk with Sonic.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:35.010
Young lady, I see that you like that boy.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.050
You can tell?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.260
I can tell just by looking at you.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.350
How embarrassing.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:48.270
Unfortunately, there's a problem. He's with Grandma Linda.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.860
Just who are you talking about?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.530
Well? Have you decided your next move?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:05.700
Young man, it's dangerous to lose patience in any battle.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:13.000
Haven't you experienced something similar in your life?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:23.390
You're right. Not only do you get yourself in trouble, but you put other people in danger too.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.180
Mister.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.890
Are you sleeping?!?

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:43.200
Those dimwits think they've defeated me because they destroyed the tower. However, my robot factory is still intact.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.910
When did he have time to make such a huge robot?

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:53.630
You can say that again. I knew about the previous Egg Fort, but I didn't think that there was another factory underneath it.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:11:01.760
That's why it's called a 'secret base' - because it contains secrets! I guess you'll never understand my thinking.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:08.350
He's no fun. Well then, let's go bully Sonic.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.310
Egg Fort II Dragons, take off!

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.230
Hold it!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:12.980
What?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:20.820
How dare you name it without my permission! But more importantly, I can understand if you named it 'Dragon,' but what's with the “S” at the end of the name?

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.740
Oh, you already named them?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:28.040
Of course. Yours is Bocoe Ship. And yours is Decoe Ship.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.790
And mine is the Super Egg Final Star PX-00!

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.670
You expect us to accept that!

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:42.590
That's not fair! Why is ours called Decoe and Bocoe while yours is called Super Egg Final Something Something 00?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:47.430
Yeah, it's wrong! Totally wrong!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.480
You're so selfish. Don't you realize how many people it took to deal with this?

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.980
The only person that had to deal with this was you.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:12:00.360
Fine, be quiet. I'll tell you all the names I came up with.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.280
How about Ace, Jack, King?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:02.910
No!

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.620
It's too ordinary.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.580
Then how about Stone, Scissors, Paper?

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.290
Are you taking this seriously?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.500
Receive, Toss, Attack!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.870
- Dr. Eggman has no vocabulary.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:11.870
We're not playing volleyball!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.620
Nozomi, Kanae, Tamae.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.750
That's old school.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:15.790
Yoki, Koto, Kiku.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.040
No one will understand that.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:23.840
We had no idea that Eggman was preparing to launch a frightening robot.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:29.140
We were more worried about Sonic.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:33.480
He was about to execute his plan.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.150
The X-Tornado?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:41.530
We didn't fly here on it this time, right?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.530
Well-built machines are like humans. They get lonely.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.910
The X-Tornado is always with you, Tails.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:59.500
I wonder if the X-Tornado is sad right now.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.840
How could I have left you behind! I'm horrible!

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.010
This is working!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.430
Is this a dream?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:15.980
What are you talking about, Amy? You know I can't keep my eyes off of you.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:21.190
When you're swinging your hammer, I think you're super cute!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:27.280
But on this cramped ship, I can't see your bravery in action.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:32.120
That beautiful, speed-filled figure of yours, Amy.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.410
Watch, Sonic!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.830
What? Amy's gone berserk?

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:43.670
That's right. Amy must also be stressed out for having to stay on this cramped ship.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:48.220
What should we do, grandpa? Should I talk to my father again?

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:52.260
Yes. We should before something bad happens.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.600
That's what Sonic told you?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:14:02.190
Yeah. He said I was the cutest when I'm swinging my hammer. Oh, what should I do?

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.780
I'm happy for you.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.780
I have a feeling that at this rate, Sonic and I will...

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.870
Sonic!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.380
This will be the end.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:30.090
That's enough. Put your pen down.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.970
Maybe I'll just draw another line here.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:32.720
Cheater!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.720
This will decide the final names!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.890
Okay!

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.770
I'm a man, so I will abide by the decision!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:44.900
Let's start the third 'This Is the Last Time We Decide On the Final Wonderful Name' lottery!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.280
But let me just draw one more line.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.400
Cheater!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.450
- Again?

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.700
Start!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.830
Right there! Stop!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.470
It's decided!

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.470
It's settled!

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.970
I'm glad!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.010
Let's see, the name in “B” is…

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:28.070
Long time no see! It's me!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:33.200
I bet you missed me. I brought a lot of bombs today.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:41.460
Even though you're hiding from me, it's pointless because I'll find you right away! Where are you? Are you over here?

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.790
You're not here?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.510
No one's here?

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:59.310
I was wondering who it was. It's that mischievous robot.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.600
Have you come to cause trouble again?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.650
Too bad, but no one's home today. You picked the wrong day to come.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:11.950
What's wrong?

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:18.790
Nobody's here! I hate being alone!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.790
Don't be silly. You just happened to come on the wrong day.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.750
But, but…

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:36.680
That's enough. Wipe your tears. Don't worry - I won't leave you all by yourself.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.890
Really?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:44.060
Really. I never lie.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.190
I won't cry anymore. Umm... Ella?

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.320
What is it?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.400
I'll give you this.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.600
Oh my!

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.870
It's floating ice.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.540
We'll soon be able to see the glaciers.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.080
Wear another layer because it's cold.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.000
Thank you, grandpa.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.670
Is Amy still angry?

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.840
Well, he did play with her emotions.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.510
What Sonic did was wrong.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:24.230
Come down here, Sonic! I thought you wanted to see me swing my hammer!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.150
You can't stay up there forever!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:32.650
Sorry, Amy! Not the hammer! I'll apologize!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.650
And just how do you intend to apologize?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.860
Amy is scary.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.200
It's best if we stay out of this.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:42.580
You're right.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.870
It's a whale!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.960
Wow!

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.960
They're over there too.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.090
Yeah! They're huge!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.800
Don't you think they look too big?

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.090
Yeah.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.100
Their shape is also strange.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:04.520
I was wondering why they weren't at home. They're on a cruise.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.190
Inexcusable!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.730
Exactly!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:11.310
How dare they have fun when we're not!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:18.450
Just when I was wondering what you guys were doing, you arrive in those machines. I'm surprised that you found us.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.950
We had to search for you because you weren't at home.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.910
Why can't you just stay in one place!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:30.170
Hey, let me talk! Stop stepping in front of me and covering me up!

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:35.130
Listen, Sonic! I'm going to unleash my pent-up feelings against you!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.670
Sounds like fun. I'll take you on!

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.380
Stop talking like that when you're running away!

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.510
Captain! There's an iceberg ahead!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:45.640
Reverse full throttle! Stop before we hit the iceberg!

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.810
The ship stopped.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.480
What's going on?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:54.690
Mr. Thorndyke! We reached the glacier! It's very beautiful!

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.070
This is not the time for that!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:07.410
Okay! Even though I'm standing on a glacier, I'm at an advantage as long as I'm not in the ocean!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:11.880
Stop bragging, Sonic! I'll show you something interesting!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:16.000
Egg Fort II has a secret.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.090
And that is...

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.050
Combine Egg Fort II!

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:22.930
Bang!

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.100
BaBang!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.640
BaBaBang!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:30.190
Scram combine Egg Fort II!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.900
Did you see that?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:43.160
Hello? What? We're too small?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.410
You can't see it, so recombine again?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.710
You should watch on a bigger TV set!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.880
Stop messing around and attack me!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.540
Sonic!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.750
What?

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.880
You're not moving.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.590
No way!

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.470
Sonic!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.220
This is fun! I'm blasting him over and over!

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.520
Sonic!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.850
Sonic, hang in there!

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:16.110
Young man, you seem to be fighting a tough battle.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:21.900
It's impossible to run fast on ice.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:27.280
Now's the time to take things slowly and carefully.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:33.330
Calm down and take things slowly step by step.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:43.800
I see. I can feel the ice with my feet.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:47.100
He's looking this way and smirking.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:50.180
That's not good. He must have figured something out.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.140
How dare that granny interfere!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.940
I'll have to punish her first!

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.400
Captain!

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.900
Messenger Robo?

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.490
What is he doing?

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.860
Let me inside.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.740
What's wrong?

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.040
X-Tornado?

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.750
Who's flying it?

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.460
Hold it, you brat!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.210
Ella?

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:18.130
Why?

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.380
When did Ella learn how to fly the X-Tornado?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:24.380
I taught her awhile back because I was bored.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.260
Here she comes!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.800
What did you do?

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.470
Change into X-Cyclone!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.270
Set up!

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:39.360
Cyclone Kick!

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.070
Why us?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:49.120
Oh no! Not again!

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:58.330
It's because you're still young. We acted the same way when we were your age.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:09.300
As time goes on, we can't tolerate overworking our bodies. But in exchange, God gives us plenty of time to think.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:17.230
He gives us time to think deeply about all the good and bad things we've done in life.

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:16.140
- Sonic!

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:20.440
We're ready. Should we go home early together?

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.360
Tails!

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:25.190
Come down.

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:29.450
We don't get to go on cruises everyday, so let's take it easy.

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:42.670
So if we do something bad, we have to think about it until the end of time.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.210 --> 00:25:35.360
Speed Match! Sonic vs Sam
